The source-body junction capacitance is determined from the junction area and the depletion width. The total junction area of the source-body junction includes the bottom area and the two sidewall areas: \[A=(0.2\,\mu\text{m}+0.2\,\mu\text{m}+0.2\,\mu\text{m})(1\,\mu\text{m})
+2(0.2\,\mu\text{m}\times0.2\,\mu\text{m})\] \[A=0.68\,\mu\text{m}^{2}
=0.68\times10^{-12}\,\text{m}^{2}\] The depletion width at the junction is \[d=10\,\text{nm}=10\times10^{-9}\,\text{m}\] The junction capacitance is \[C_s=\frac{\varepsilon_r\varepsilon_0 A}{d}\] Using \(\varepsilon_r=11.7\) for silicon and \(\varepsilon_0=8.9\times10^{-12}\,\text{F/m}\), \[C_s=
\frac{(11.7)(8.9\times10^{-12})(0.68\times10^{-12})}
{10\times10^{-9}}\] \[C_s\approx7\times10^{-15}\,\text{F}
=7\,\text{fF}\] \[\boxed{\text{(B) }7\,\text{fF}}\]

